A solitary figure sits in lotus position atop a translucent, iridescent soap bubble floating in an infinite cosmic void, their form gradually dissolving into swirling particles that drift outward like dandelion seeds. Inside the bubble, fragmented scenes of lightning storms, ancient temples, and scientific equations orbit chaotically. Outside the bubble membrane, the space transforms into pure luminous negative space—neither dark nor light, but an impossible color that suggests infinite potential. The figure's dissolving edges blend seamlessly with both the interior chaos and exterior void, creating ambiguity about where the observer ends and the observed begins. Style of Marc Chagall: dreamlike floating composition, rich jewel tones of deep sapphire and amber against ethereal whites, mystical folk-art sensibility with figures defying gravity, soft painterly brushwork with areas of transparent color washes, emotional rather than literal spatial relationships.
